       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in takotsubo:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " NTG lowers LV and RV filling pressures and afterload in acute HF; avoid it w LVOTO (it worsens the pressure gradient)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Also contraindicated w sGC stimulators such as riociguat (hypotension)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated in severe anemia (methemoglobin can worsen it). May aggravate angina from HCM. Severe hypotension can occur even w sm doses, esp w aortic or MS, constrictive pericarditis, vol depletion or existing hypotension."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe hypotension, throbbing HA, methemoglobinemia w cyanosis, syncope. ⍉specific antagonist: raise central fluid vol (shock position, IV saline); methylene blue 1–2 mg/kg IV for methemoglobinemia unless G6PD deficiency; Epi = ineffective."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
